{title: Seraiah Was Secretary}
{subtitle: 2 Samuel 8:17; 8:15–18; 1 Chronicles 18:16; 2 Samuel 8:16–17}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
David reigned over all the land
Justice [Eb]and righteousness in his hand
He se[F]cured the kingdom's peace
And placed [Gm]his servants in their place
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Joab over the army stood
Je[Eb]hoshaphat recorded the word
[F]Zadok and Ahimelech served
Priests [Gm]to the Lord they preserved
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sera[Bb]iah was secretary
[F]Writing [Gm]the king's de[Eb]cree
In the [Bb]register of the great
[F]His name is set in the [Eb]text
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Be[Gm]naiah over the Kerethites
And [Eb]David's sons were priests
An [F]organized house of rule
Where every [Gm]duty is fulfilled
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Shavsha in Chronicles appears
[Eb]The same scribe, different name
[F]Documenting the royal word
In the sta[Gm]bility of the Lord
{end_of_bridge}

